---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '2026-10-24';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="How PromptDNS content is produced and verified: primary-source checking against RFCs and vendor docs, labeled synthetic examples, and public corrections."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Editorial policy</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-faint">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>How content is produced</h2>
      <p>
        PromptDNS is produced with AI assistance and verified against primary sources before
        publication: RFCs for protocol behaviour (7208 for SPF, 7489 for DMARC, 6376 for DKIM,
        8460/8461 for TLS reporting and MTA-STS) and the vendor's own documentation for
        provider-specific steps and record values.
      </p>

      <h2>Standards we hold pages to</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Primary sources over paraphrase.</strong> Where a rule matters (lookup limits, alignment modes, policy semantics), the RFC is cited and linked.</li>
        <li><strong>Labeled examples.</strong> Worked examples use reserved example domains and are marked as illustrative; we do not present synthetic data as observed data.</li>
        <li><strong>No guaranteed verdicts about receivers.</strong> Mail reception is every receiver's decision; our pages say what a record <em>permits receivers to conclude</em>, not what they will definitely do.</li>
        <li><strong>Honest tool scope.</strong> Each tool states what it inspects and what it cannot see.</li>
        <li><strong>No invented facts.</strong> If a provider's exact include string or limit isn't verified, the page says how to find it rather than guessing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Pages are revisited when the underlying specification or provider guidance changes, and
        when readers report problems. Significant corrections are published on the
        <a href="/changelog/" class="text-accent">changelog</a> rather than quietly edited.
        To report an error: <a href="mailto:bugs@promptdns.com" class="text-accent">bugs@promptdns.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        Comparison and recommendation pages, as they are published, state their criteria and the
        date prices were checked, and name where competitors beat us. We do not accept payment
        for coverage.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
